sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: From a given point to draw a straight line touching a given circle.
----
proof:

Let {A} be the given point, and {BCD} the given circle.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="280" height="280" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="III.17 diagram" src="propIII17.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // A CONSTRUCTION: the tangent from an outside point. The apparatus —
    // center, join, the outer circle, the perpendicular at D, the two
    // joins — is shown one animated step per clause; III.1 is assumed per
    // the fatigue rule and E simply appears.
    //
    // Joyce's outer circle is declared first and carries a random fill,
    // with the given circle BCD filled on top of it. A highlighted element
    // is promoted within its draw pass (#140), so lighting that circle —
    // from a slide set or a {AFG} hover — would paint its face over BCD's.
    // It is therefore renamed AFGfill, never named in a slide set, and a
    // fully transparent twin AFG carries the name for prose and captions.
    // The compass animation is safe on AFGfill itself: its face fades in
    // only after drawProgress has finalised, when the element is no longer
    // promoted, so BCD stays on top throughout.
    //
    // Everything else added is fully transparent (;0;0;0 lines, ;0;0;0;0
    // polygons and circle), so the static figure is unchanged: ED and EB
    // are the radii of BCD the I.4 step compares (AE and FE already draw
    // them), DEF and BEA the two triangles, and three angle markers — the
    // right angles at D and B in red, and the angle at E they share.
    // B is a letter of the given circle's name, so it stands with C and D
    // from the first slide even though the construction only reaches it
    // ("make EB equal to ED") later: a derived point, listed here, not deferred.
    var GIVEN = ["A","BCD","B","C","D"];
    var CENT  = GIVEN.concat(["E","AE"]);
    // F, like G, is a letter of the circle's name AFG and stands with it
    // from the moment the circle is described; it is a derived point (the
    // perpendicular's end), so it is listed here, not deferred.
    var CIRC  = CENT.concat(["AFGfill","AFG","F","G"]);
    var PERP  = CIRC.concat(["F","FD","angEDF"]);
    var JOIN  = PERP.concat(["FE","B","BA"]);
    var RADII = JOIN.concat(["ED","EB"]);
    var ANGE  = RADII.concat(["angAEF"]);
    var TRI   = ANGE.concat(["DEF","BEA"]);
    var RT    = TRI.concat(["angEBA"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "III.17",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;140,40",
            "E;point;free;140,150",
            "D;point;lineSlider;A,E,140,90",
            // Joyce's AFG, renamed: see the note above.
            "AFGfill;circle;radius;E,A;0;0;black;random",
            "AFG;circle;radius;E,A;0;0;0;0",
            "BCD;circle;radius;E,D;0;0;black;random",
            "C;point;circleSlider;BCD,230,160;black;0",
            "G;point;circleSlider;AFGfill,220,220;black;0",
            "AE;line;connect;A,E",
            "DF';line;perpendicular;D,E;0;0;0",
            "FF';line;chord;DF',AFGfill;0;0;0",
            "F;point;first;FF'",
            "FD;line;connect;F,D",
            "FE;line;connect;F,E",
            "B;point;cutoff;E,F,E,D",
            "BA;line;connect;B,A",
            // Hover / highlight targets only — AE and FE already draw these.
            "ED;line;connect;E,D;0;0;0",
            "EB;line;connect;E,B;0;0;0",
            "DEF;polygon;triangle;D,E,F;0;0;0;0",
            "BEA;polygon;triangle;B,E,A;0;0;0;0",
            "angEDF;sector;angleMarkerRight;D,E,F;0;0;red;red",
            "angAEF;sector;angleMarker;E,A,F",
            "angEBA;sector;angleMarkerRight;B,E,A;0;0;red;red"
        ],
        // Draggable, checked against the bundle: A, E, D, C, G. E is the
        // center the proof takes on its first construction step and G the
        // letter the outer circle brings with it, so both are deferred to
        // follow `visible`. A is the given point; C and D are letters of
        // the given circle, so they belong on slide 1. F (first) and B
        // (cutoff) are derived, hence listed per slide. The resting figure
        // is unaffected.
        deferDraggables: ["E","G"],
        aliases: { "EA": "AE", "DF": "FD", "EF": "FE", "AB": "BA",
                   "DE": "ED", "BE": "EB",
                   "EDF": "angEDF", "FDE": "angEDF",
                   "AEF": "angAEF", "FEA": "angAEF",
                   "EBA": "angEBA", "ABE": "angEBA" },
        slides: [
            // The deck opens on the proposition's statement over the givens
            // (process.md “Open on the statement”).
            { text: "From a given point to draw a straight line touching a given circle.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: [],
              justifications: [{ ref: "III.17" }] },
            { text: "Let {A} be the given point, and {BCD} the given circle.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["A","BCD"] },
            { text: "It is required to draw from the point {A} a straight line touching the circle {BCD}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["A","BCD"] },
            { text: "Take the center {E} of the circle, and join {AE}.",
              visible: CENT,
              highlighted: ["E", "AE"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "E",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "AE", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [
                  { claim: "the center E of the circle", ref: "III.1" },
                  { ref: "I.Post.1" } ] },
            { text: "Describe the circle {AFG} with center {E} and radius {EA}.",
              visible: CIRC,
              highlighted: ["E","AE"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "AFGfill", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "the circle with center E and radius EA", ref: "I.Post.3" }] },
            { text: "Draw {DF} from {D} at right angles to {EA}.",
              visible: PERP,
              highlighted: ["D","AE"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "F",      name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "FD",     name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "angEDF", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "DF at right angles to EA", ref: "I.11" }] },
            { text: "Join {EF} and {AB}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: [],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "FE", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "B",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "BA", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "I say that {AB} has been drawn from the point {A} touching the circle {BCD}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["BA","A","BCD"] },
            // His sentence pairs two equalities; one slide each so the gold
            // shows one pair of radii at a time.
            { text: "For, since {E} is the center of the circles {BCD} and {AFG}, {EA} equals {EF},",
              visible: RADII,
              highlighted: ["E","AE","FE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "radii of the circle AFG", ref: "I.Def.15" }] },
            { text: "and {ED} equals {EB}.",
              visible: RADII,
              highlighted: ["E","ED","EB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "radii of the circle BCD", ref: "I.Def.15" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the two sides {AE} and {EB} equal the two sides {FE} and {ED}, and they contain a common angle, the angle at {E},",
              visible: ANGE,
              highlighted: ["AE","EB","FE","ED"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angAEF", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "therefore the base {DF} equals the base {AB}, and the triangle {DEF} equals the triangle {BEA},",
              visible: TRI,
              highlighted: ["FD","BA","DEF","BEA"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "two sides and the contained angle equal", ref: "I.4" }] },
            { text: "and the remaining angles to the remaining angles, therefore the angle {EDF} equals the angle {EBA}.",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["angEDF"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angEBA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "the remaining angles opposite the equal sides", ref: "I.4" }] },
            { text: "But the angle {EDF} is right, therefore the angle {EBA} is also right.",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["angEDF","angEBA"] },
            { text: "Now {EB} is a radius, and the straight line drawn at right angles to the diameter of a circle, from its end, touches the circle, therefore {AB} touches the circle {BCD}.",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["EB","angEBA","BA","BCD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "at right angles to the diameter from its end", ref: "III.16.Cor" }] },
            { text: "Therefore from the given point {A} the straight line {AB} has been drawn touching the circle {BCD}.",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["A","BA","BCD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.F." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "III.17") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.1":   "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.Post.3":   "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post3/",
        "I.Def.15":   "/elements/books/bookI/definitions/defI15/",
        "I.4":        "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI4/",
        "I.11":       "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI11/",
        "III.1":      "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII1/",
        "III.16.Cor": "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII16/#cor"
    });
</script>
</figure>

It is required to draw from the point {A} a straight line touching the circle {BCD}.

Take the center {E} of the circle, and join {AE}.  Describe the circle {AFG} with center {E} and radius {EA}.  Draw {DF} from {D} at right angles to {EA}.  Join {EF} and {AB}. [!just III.1; I.11]

I say that {AB} has been drawn from the point {A} touching the circle {BCD}.

For, since {E} is the center of the circles {BCD} and {AFG}, {EA} equals {EF}, and {ED} equals {EB}.  Therefore the two sides {AE} and {EB} equal the two sides {FE} and {ED}, and they contain a common angle, the angle at {E}, therefore the base {DF} equals the base {AB}, and the triangle {DEF} equals the triangle {BEA}, and the remaining angles to the remaining angles, therefore the angle {EDF} equals the angle {EBA}. [!just I.4]

But the angle {EDF} is right, therefore the angle {EBA} is also right.

Now {EB} is a radius, and the straight line drawn at right angles to the diameter of a circle, from its end, touches the circle, therefore {AB} touches the circle {BCD}. [!just III.16.Cor]

Therefore from the given point {A} the straight line {AB} has been drawn touching the circle {BCD}.

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
<br clear="all">
